# 🚑 Ambulance Dispatch & Emergency Response Simulator

## 📌 Project Overview

The Ambulance Dispatch & Emergency Response Simulator is a C++ based
emergency management system that simulates how an emergency control
center can receive emergency requests, prioritize them, select a suitable
ambulance, find an appropriate hospital, and manage the emergency lifecycle.

The project demonstrates Object-Oriented Programming, STL containers,
priority queues, distance calculation, file handling, exception handling,
and algorithmic decision making.

---

## 🎯 Objectives

- Manage emergency requests
- Prioritize emergencies based on severity
- Maintain ambulance information
- Maintain hospital information
- Match ambulances with required equipment
- Calculate ambulance distance
- Select suitable hospitals
- Dispatch emergency vehicles
- Track emergency status
- Generate emergency reports

---

## 🚨 Emergency Priority

| Priority | Severity |
|----------|----------|
| 1 | Critical |
| 2 | High |
| 3 | Medium |
| 4 | Low |

Critical emergencies are processed before lower-priority emergencies.

---

## 🚑 Ambulance Types

- Basic Ambulance
- Advanced Ambulance
- ICU Ambulance

The system considers ambulance availability and required equipment
before dispatching.

---

## 🏥 Hospital Selection

Hospitals are selected using:

- Emergency bed availability
- ICU bed availability
- Required department
- Distance from emergency location

---

## 🧠 System Workflow

Emergency Reported
↓
Priority Assignment
↓
Available Ambulance Search
↓
Equipment Matching
↓
Distance Calculation
↓
Ambulance Selection
↓
Hospital Selection
↓
Emergency Dispatch
↓
Patient Transport
↓
Emergency Completion
↓
Report Generation

